<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ryazan</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Pereyaslavl-Ryazansky</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ryazan is a city in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> on the Oka river, south-east of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a>. Called Pereyaslavl-Ryazansky until 1778, it replaced Old Ryazan, destroyed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a> in 1237, as the seat of the princes of Ryazan in the fourteenth century. The principality was annexed by Moscow in 1521, and the city keeps its kremlin with the Dormition Cathedral.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ryazan.jpg" alt="Ryazan" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ted.ns · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%D0%A4%D0%B5%D1%81%D1%82%D0%B8%D0%B2%D0%B0%D0%BB%D1%8C_%D0%B2%D0%BE%D0%B7%D0%B4%D1%83%D1%85%D0%BE%D0%BF%D0%BB%D0%B0%D0%B2%D0%B0%D0%BD%D0%B8%D1%8F_%D0%B2_%D0%A0%D1%8F%D0%B7%D0%B0%D0%BD%D0%B8.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
